{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form","id":759001,"title":"The Father's Form","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T10:41:30-08:00","id":759001,"title":"The Father's Form","content":"Been reading through the Werewolf book over the last while. Really enjoying it and most of the Gifts are pretty awesome. Except this one. I just can't understand what purpose it serves. At first I thought it was a way of assuming a Combat form not quite on par with Gauru that you get more time with, but pretty much as soon as combat begins, you're going to end up following the regular Gauru rules anyway. Then I thought it was a way of Cheesing a few extra rounds of Gauru, by forcing the transformation a second time, but it doesn't say that anything resets, so you probably just end up entering Basu-Im as soon as you get into combat.<br /> <br /> Then I thought that it was a utility gift, but your Stamina is on par with Urshul and the Urshul is actually faster. I suppose it can be used when you need that extra dot of strength, but there are other gifts to grant you strength anyway, and if there is that much disparity between yourself and the object, you're probably not going to move it anyway.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts and suggestions? Stuff I might have missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6351-kaoleth","name":"Kaoleth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:00:04-08:00","id":759062,"title":"","content":"I was going to say something about Lunacy, but then it says that it causes Lunacy as if you were in Urshul form.<br /> <br /> I guess it's a way to get a bonus to Strength, Size, and Dexterity and keep opposable (albeit big and unwieldy) thumbs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:46:27-08:00","id":759099,"title":"","content":"The benefits are more cultural then mechanical. It isn't about being a murder monster. It's about purity and your composure to the resident of the hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T11:53:22-08:00","id":759102,"title":"","content":"Some people want to be able to lounge around in gauru form without having to attack people. I would have preferred it to be an optional rule and we'd have a more fitting gift in its place, but I'm not one of those people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:07:09-08:00","id":759123,"title":"","content":"I actually read it as &quot;Here, have a free Breaking Point Towards Flesh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T12:11:45-08:00","id":759127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759062#post759062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it's a way to get a bonus to Strength, Size, and Dexterity and keep opposable (albeit big and unwieldy) thumbs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget the +1 Perception as well. Gauru form has the biggest attribute bonuses of any form, plus opposable thumbs, which would make it the ideal form for performing Rites if not for the built-in countdown timer to Death Rage. Father's form fixes that problem.<br /> <br /> It's also a great intimidation tactic. Gauru is called the Killing Form for a reason, and taking it shows that you are willing to use deadly force, possibly even to risk <i>Kuruth</i>. Father's Form allows you to pose as the guy who's willing to kill you to win an argument, without actually risking Death Rage unless a fight breaks out.<br /> <br /> And, as Lyrics of War pointed out, there's huge cultural significance to being able to enter was believed to be Father Wolf's true form at any time, and sustain it without losing control.<br /> <br /> Still, it's not to everyone's taste, so I homebrewed <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/492158-homebrewed-primal-form-facet#post492158\">an alternative Facet</a> for those who don't care for Father's Form, inspired by 1e's Primal Form Gift. In my games, it's actually a Fetish that allows you to use Father's Form in an alternate way, but it works as a replacement as well if you don't like Father's Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:42:06-08:00","id":759621,"title":"","content":"I'm voting for cultural / role play reasons here. I mean, is there a significant reason to take Luna's Embrace beyond the story potential? I've never seen anyone take Beast Talker or similar when you could be talking to more knowledgable spirits instead. I've only seen Skin Thief used when I had a fellow player want to run around as a non-wolf shifter for a while, and never used with another human being. <br /> <br /> There are plenty of Gifts who's sole purpose revolves around story. And, about 3 times of 10, I see those Gifts picked up more than the &quot;useful&quot; ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:57:23-08:00","id":759657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759621#post759621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm voting for cultural / role play reasons here. I mean, is there a significant reason to take Luna's Embrace beyond the story potential?</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes for a damned good disguise that doesn't require the skins of people and still allows for shapeshifting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T23:28:43-08:00","id":759773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759621#post759621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never seen anyone take Beast Talker or similar when you could be talking to more knowledgable spirits instead. I've only seen Skin Thief used when I had a fellow player want to run around as a non-wolf shifter for a while, and never used with another human being.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of Gifts who's sole purpose revolves around story. And, about 3 times of 10, I see those Gifts picked up more than the &quot;useful&quot; ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>@Beast Talker: Contacts (Local Fauna) is a -great- way to know when something is going wrong with your territory. Hosts? Check. God Machine Infrastructure that specifically fucks with their environment? Check.<br /> <br /> @Skin Thief: My Irraka was super happy with the fetish knife that let her preserve some of the (human) skins she gets. Let's be honest, it'd see way more play if you could impersonate someone more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T01:39:25-08:00","id":759828,"title":"","content":"It lets you take Gauru as a favored form and still apply your exceptional success on 3 to a non-combat facet, which often have more to gain from it. Plus it's the best form for any gift where you roll strength, like Flesh of Earth. And of course, fetishes modifying the effects of gifts is a thing. <br /> <br /> Also, climbing. Just seems like something gauru form would do better than urshul, what with being more ape-shaped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:58:43-08:00","id":759901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759773#post759773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Beast Talker: Contacts (Local Fauna) is a -great- way to know when something is going wrong with your territory. Hosts? Check. God Machine Infrastructure that specifically fucks with their environment? Check.<br /> <br /> @Skin Thief: My Irraka was super happy with the fetish knife that let her preserve some of the (human) skins she gets. Let's be honest, it'd see way more play if you could impersonate someone more than once.</div> </div> </div> </div> Contacts (Local Spirits) is just as effective, if not more so, plus it doesn't require a Gift first. And your Irraka was using a homebrew fetish, not the Gift as written - I'm talking about using things by default. And I've seen people use Skin Thief as is for the fluff potential.<br /> <br /> People use Gifts because they like the flavor, not because they're trying to crunch out the ultimate in something. While the latter is a valid playstyle, its hardly the only one in existance, and lots of people don't worry about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:46:21-08:00","id":759924,"title":"","content":"I think the real application of Beast talker is things like commanding an army of grizzly bears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T07:33:21-08:00","id":759974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759901#post759901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Contacts (Local Spirits) is just as effective, if not more so, plus it doesn't require a Gift first. And your Irraka was using a homebrew fetish, not the Gift as written - I'm talking about using things by default. And I've seen people use Skin Thief as is for the fluff potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it doesn't requires stupid amounts of Gathra and/or essence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T09:12:47-08:00","id":760019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=759901#post759901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Contacts (Local Spirits) is just as effective, if not more so, plus it doesn't require a Gift first.</div> </div> </div> </div>They cost the same in experience and you can have both.<br /> <br /> Beast Talker is useful for speaking with animal members of packs, as Elfive pointed out, but also getting past 'guard' animals, dealing with familiars and animal members of other packs. Plus local spirits tend to be stuck on one side of the Gauntlet, the spirit side. Having Beast Talker to deal with things on the flesh side is a valid use, especially since not all enemies will be hosts with a noticeable impact on the spirit side of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:36:59-08:00","id":760222,"title":"","content":"Page 287 of WtF2nd has a fairly lengthy explanation of the intent meant for the gift, as well as some alternate rule suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T00:04:24-08:00","id":760546,"title":"","content":"Let's just admit that when all else is done and everything being equal, sometimes we pick something just because it's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T05:33:34-08:00","id":760619,"title":"","content":"Right? I absolutely hate when people try to limit things because they don't see a &quot;mechanical benefit.&quot; <br /> <br /> Reminds me of all the nerf crying on destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T11:20:34-08:00","id":760778,"title":"","content":"There is one obvious advantage. Even. The whimpers wolves get to have Olympic tier heavy lifting while still having opposable thumbs <br /> <br /> <br /> Groceries have never been easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T19:18:46-08:00","id":761134,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hun can you bring in dinner? The one for the pack?&quot; &quot;Sure dear!&quot; -hefts a recently slaughtered moose-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","t