":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=762440#post762440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but they might be going for the 'Wolfman's got Nards!' achievement.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how you gain Glory renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:52:34-08:00","id":762617,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to think there might be other difficulties inherent in Gauru sexy times even if they do have genitalia. I mean, what kind of birth control would even work with that? Hormonal birth control might not work depending on biology, they don't make gauru sized condoms, and if the males have knots then they can't pull out... so, unless gauru form's reproductive cycle is more like a wolf's then like a human's (maybe going into &quot;season&quot; sometime around Lupercalia/ Valentine's day (That's how the werewolves in the novel I'm writing work, at least, so I feel it could work) then there would be a lot of unintended pregnancy from that...<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, would the fetus change shape with the mother? I know blood of the wolf says no, but that doesn't make sense to me and it may well have changed in 2nd edition. I think the fetus would piggyback on the mothers' shape-shifting but not be able to shift by itself (at least until after it's born and either a shape-shifting tell manifests or it goes through the first change, and then the momma werewolf instinctively shifts to hishu when labor begins. urban legends where the mother somehow doesn't shift back to hishu, (resulting in babies born in another form and unable to enter hishu until the first change) not withstanding (these rumors also claim that the predator kings deliberately do this so that the child never has the stink of being human.<br /> <br /> The other reason I view that way is because this:<img src=\"http://pre03.deviantart.net/02e0/th/pre/i/2010/281/0/4/werewolf_fetus_in_a_jar1_by_shadechristiwolven-d30cpfo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> would be an awesome LARP prop to be sitting on some Cheiron group or Null Mysteriis hunter's shelf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:00:26-08:00","id":762625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/759001-the-father-s-form?p=762617#post762617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to think there might be other difficulties inherent in Gauru sexy times even if they do have genitalia. I mean, what kind of birth control would even work with that? Hormonal birth control might not work depending on biology, they don't make gauru sized condoms, and if the males have knots then they can't pull out... so, unless gauru form's reproductive cycle is more like a wolf's then like a human's ... then there would be a lot of unintended pregnancy from that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most werewolves likely don't have Father's Form, even fewer of those probably use it to have sex. And the werewolves who don't definitely don't use gauru for sex. The amount of 'unintended pregnancies' is probably no higher than your average mortal population.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, would the fetus change shape with the mother? I know blood of the wolf says no, but that doesn't make sense to me and it may well have changed in 2nd edition. I think the fetus would piggyback on the mothers' shape-shifting but not be able to shift by itself (at least until after it's born and either a shape-shifting tell manifests or it goes through the first change, and then the momma werewolf instinctively shifts to hishu when labor begins. urban legends where the mother somehow doesn't shift back to hishu, (resulting in babies born in another form and unable to enter hishu until the first change) not withstanding (these rumors also claim that the predator kings deliberately do this so that the child never has the stink of being human. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully they'll never get into details for reasons expressed above. Blood of the Wolf is the kind of book we don't need to see retread, except perhaps the Wolf-Blooded section. But I imagine fetus gets safely held in the innerspace where a werewolf's massive amount of extra flesh goes when it's not in one of the larger forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-10-2015, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:07:27-08:00","id":762631,"title":"","content":"This is obviously not a dev call, but I really doubt it needs to be one, so for the sake of everyones' sanity assume that Uratha in Gauru cannot engage in sexual intercourse. I certainly do not intend to ever write material for W:tF involving Gauru getting hot and heavy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio